course: dictionary
lesson: 9272
title: Spaceship
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spaceship is a vehicle that can travel in space. Its job is to carry things or people beyond the air around Earth. «Max got a Lego set for his birthday; his brother built the spaceship from it.» Here the spaceship is a model made from bricks, not a real vehicle.
explain: Look at the two parts of the word: space and ship. A ship is a vehicle that travels, and space is the great empty place beyond the sky. Put them together and you get a vehicle for space. The dictionary says it is often one with people inside, like a home for astronauts on a trip.
explain: Check your meaning in a sentence. «Oliver said sorry, and on Saturday he played with Alfie the whole morning — the rocket, two spaceships and a moon base.» Swap in "toy vehicles for space" and it still makes sense, so the context tells you these are toys. Always ask whether the context shows a real vehicle or a model.
fact: A spaceship is a vehicle that can travel in space, especially one with people inside.
fact: Spaceship is a noun: one spaceship, two spaceships.
fact: In science lessons you learn about rockets, space shuttles and the International Space Station.
fact: Useful phrases are build a spaceship, board the spaceship and alien spaceship.
fact: In a story, spaceship can mean a real vehicle or a toy model. The context tells you which.
exercise: «Max got a Lego set; his brother built the spaceship from it.» What is the spaceship in this sentence? | A loud noise in the night | A kind of pizza | *A model made from bricks | A bird that flies over the sea
exercise: A spaceship is best described as: | A building with a shop on the roof | A boat that sails on lakes | *A vehicle that can travel in space | A type of planet
exercise: Which phrase from the lessons means getting onto a spaceship? | build a spaceship | *board the spaceship | alien spaceship | moon base
test: «A boy in Ohio cannot finish his Lego spaceship; he looks at the instructions again and spots a missing piece on page 12.» What does looking at the instructions help him do? | *Find the missing piece and finish the ship | Eat his drink | Fly to the moon | Give up forever
test: Which is the correct plural of spaceship? | spaceses | spaceship | *spaceships | spaceshipes
exam: Which sentence shows spaceship as a real vehicle, not a toy? | The box showed a spaceship on the front | Oliver played with two spaceships in the garden | Max built a spaceship from bricks on the carpet | *The astronauts boarded the spaceship at the launch pad
